Article 40
(1) In an effort to provide and organize handling of services and protection for victims, PPT establishes FPKK.
(2) FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) aims to: a. coordinate and synchronize the handling of PPT services;
b. maintain and develop networks and referral systems; and c. collect, compile and present reports on violence.
(3) The management and membership of FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be determined by Decree of the Chairperson of PTT.
(4) The membership of FPKK as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be grouped in the following roles:
a. health role;
b. psychology role;
c. legal role;
d. social role; and
e. economic role.
(5) Further provisions regarding the establishment, main duties, and functions as well as membership of FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 41
(1) Dalam rangka mencapai tujuan perlindungan anak dan perempuan dari  tindak kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 3, Pemerintah  Daerah bekerjasama dengan:
a. Pemerintah;
b. Pemerintah Provinsi;
c. Kabupaten/Kota lain; dan
d. lembaga non Pemerintah.
(2) Kerja sama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi: a. pertukaran data dan informasi;
b. rehabilitasi korban tindak kekerasan;
c. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial; dan
d. penyediaan barang bukti dan saksi, serta ditindaklanjuti sesuai dengan  hukum yang berlaku.
(3) Kerjasama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dan ayat (2) dituangkan  dalam bentuk Kesepakatan Bersama.

